{"body":"## Problem\n\nFour merge tombstones from the 2026-09-21 semantic review (#722) still carry their **old, rejected identity** as `identifier`, not their merge target:\n\n| record | `identifier` (published) | merged into (per its `MERGED_INTO` event) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Nano.yaml` (label `NaNO`) | `NCIT:C54713`, the *nano* unit prefix | `CHEBI:63005` (NaNO3) |\n| `Atrazin.yaml` | `cas:1924-24-9` (an erroneous CAS) | `CHEBI:15930` (atrazine) |\n| `Edta_Chelating_Agent.yaml` | `NCIT:C360` (chelating agents, a class) | `CHEBI:4735` (EDTA) |\n| `Sodium_Phosphate_Dibasic.yaml` | `CHEBI:37583` (trisodium phosphate) | `CHEBI:34683` (Na2HPO4) |\n\n`docs/LABEL_INDEX_CONTRACT.md` says: *\"For a **merged** record the `identifier` already points at the merge target, so the row still resolves correctly and should be followed.\"* These four rows break that rule. A consumer that follows REJECTED rows, as the contract tells it to, resolves `NaNO` to the nano prefix and `Sodium phosphate dibasic` to trisodium phosphate. No live MAPPED row holds any of the four identifiers.\n\n## How it surfaced\n\nCultureMech's label-index reader refuses a pin with dangling tombstones. Once CultureBotAI/CultureMech#520 lets it read `AMBIGUOUS` rows, a preview refresh against MIM `7a65c4e9` fails with:\n\n```\nLabelIndexError: REJECTED merge tombstone identifier is not held by a live MAPPED row: CHEBI:37583, NCIT:C360, NCIT:C54713, cas:1924-24-9\n```\n\nSo this now blocks CultureMech's MIM pin, which is 106 commits behind.\n\n## Proposed fix\n\nPoint each tombstone's `identifier` at its merge target. Keep the original fields on the tombstone, as the merge events say they should be kept, and record the old identifier in the `curation_history` event. Every one of these record changes needs a `mapping_changes/` receipt through the review chain. Also add a MIM-side gate so a merge tombstone whose identifier no live record holds can't land (CultureMech already enforces this as a consumer).\n","comments":[],"number":799,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Four 2026-09-21 merge tombstones keep their rejected identity instead of the merge target, breaking the label-index contract","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/799"}
